						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MINIMAL 2D CLONER TEMPLATE\n\nThis patch shows the essential building blocks for a cloner effect.\nWe start with a Rectangle mesh that adheres to the aspect ratio of the patch.\nThis is to match the aspect ratio of the Texture In, preventing squashing of the image.\n\nThe mesh receives its transformation data from the Transformation 2D node, which is fed coordinates by the Grid Pattern node.\nIn this example we are using the Grid Pattern node, but you could use other patterns, random data, manual coordinates etc.\n \nThe Texture In provides us with the image you apply the effect on in Arena\/Avenue.\nWe use the Wire logo as placeholder, but this image will be replaced with your clip in Arena\/Avenue."
					}
				},
